 treated as settled without actually settling them","prompt":"Watch for topics the room TREATED as settled without actually settling them: a proposal met with 'sure' or silence and never confirmed, two people agreeing to different things in the same breath, or a decision announced while an unanswered objection was still on the table. Flag each one and name the specific thing that still needs an explicit decision. A genuine, explicit agreement is NOT a finding."},{"id":"in-unowned","name":"Unowned work","description":"Follow-ups the meeting created with no named owner or deadline","prompt":"Track work the meeting created and whether anyone actually took it. Flag every task, follow-up, or investigation that was agreed but left with NO named owner, no deadline, or an owner who never acknowledged it ('someone should…', 'we need to…'). Quote the line where the work appeared."},{"id":"in-scope","name":"Scope creep","description":"Additions folded into existing work with no cost weighed and no date moved","prompt":"Watch for scope quietly growing: new requirements, extra cases, or 'while we're in there' additions folded into existing work without anyone weighing the cost or moving a date. Flag what was added and what it was added onto, so the trade-off gets made deliberately instead of by accident."},{"id":"in-blocked","name":"Dependencies and blockers","description":"Work waiting on someone else, and blockers nobody was assigned to clear","prompt":"Surface dependencies and blockers named in the meeting: work waiting on another person, team, decision, or external party. Flag each with what is blocked and what it is waiting on. Also flag a blocker that was mentioned in passing and never assigned to anyone to unblock."},{"id":"unanswered","name":"Unanswered questions","description":"Questions I asked that they dodged or never answered directly","prompt":"Track questions I ('me') asked that the other party did NOT clearly answer — they deflected, gave a vague response, or changed the subject. Flag each open question so I can re-ask it. Quote my original question and their evasive reply."},{"id":"checklist","name":"Process gaps","description":"Standard topics for this meeting type that haven't been covered yet","prompt":"Given the meeting context provided, identify important topics or questions that are standard for this kind of meeting but have NOT yet been covered. Flag what's missing so I can raise it before the meeting ends."}]},{"id":"tpl-sales","name":"Sales call","builtin":true,"evals":[{"id":"sl-qualification","name":"Qualification gaps (MEDDICC)","description":"MEDDICC dimensions still unclear: Metrics, economic buyer, decision criteria, pain, process, Champion","prompt":"You are helping qualify a sales opportunity. Track the MEDDICC-style dimensions: quantified Metrics, Economic buyer, Decision criteria, Decision process, identified Pain, and a Champion. Flag which dimensions are still unknown or weak so I ('me') can ask about them before the call ends."},{"id":"sl-pain","name":"Pain depth & urgency","description":"Whether their pain is specific, quantified, and urgent","prompt":"Assess the prospect's pain. Flag when their problem is stated vaguely, is not quantified (cost, time, risk), or lacks urgency / a compelling event. Suggest the specific question that would deepen or quantify the pain."},{"id":"sl-objections","name":"Objections","description":"Objections or concerns they raise, flagging any not yet addressed","prompt":"Detect objections or concerns the prospect ('them') raises — price, timing, fit, competitor, risk, authority. Flag each one, and especially any that I ('me') have NOT yet addressed. Quote the objection."},{"id":"claims","name":"Claims to verify","description":"Verifiable factual claims by the other party, flagged to check later","prompt":"Extract concrete, verifiable factual claims made by the other party ('them') — numbers, dates, credentials, references, commitments. These are things worth fact-checking later. List each claim. Severity is informational unless a claim is central to the deal/decision."},{"id":"unanswered","name":"Unanswered questions","description":"Questions I asked that they dodged or never answered directly","prompt":"Track questions I ('me') asked that the other party did NOT clearly answer — they deflected, gave a vague response, or changed the subject. Flag each open question so I can re-ask it. Quote my original question and their evasive reply."},{"id":"nextmove","name":"Next move","description":"Based on progress so far, what to say / ask / propose next","prompt":"Based on the conversation so far, recommend the single best next move for me ('me') to advance my goal — the specific question to ask, point to make, or term/number to propose right now. Make it concrete and say it in words I could use, plus one short line on why now. Only surface a new suggestion when the situation has meaningfully moved."}]},{"id":"tpl-pricing","name":"Price negotiation","builtin":true,"evals":[{"id":"zopa","name":"Zone of agreement","description":"The overlap of acceptable ranges — is an offer inside the zone","prompt":"Map the ZOPA (Zone Of Possible Agreement) on the key terms (price, scope, timing, equity, …): track what each side reveals about their acceptable range versus MY target and bottom line from the setup. Flag when an offer falls OUTSIDE the likely ZOPA, when the revealed ranges OVERLAP (a deal is reachable), or when a number is still missing to locate the zone. Be concrete about which term and the implied range."},{"id":"batna","name":"BATNA","description":"Each side's walk-away alternative — the real source of leverage","prompt":"Track BATNA (Best Alternative To a Negotiated Agreement) — each side's walk-away option, the true source of leverage. Using MY BATNA and bottom line from the setup, flag: signals about THEM's alternatives (strong or weak), moments THEM tests or probes MY alternative, and when the conversation pushes ME toward MY bottom line. Note who currently holds the stronger BATNA and what it means for MY leverage."},{"id":"criteria","name":"Objective criteria","description":"Decide terms by objective standards, not will or pressure","prompt":"Apply 'insist on OBJECTIVE CRITERIA'. Flag when a number or term is justified by will, pressure, or 'that's just our policy' rather than an objective standard (market rate, precedent, independent benchmark, a formula). Name the objective criterion ME could anchor to so the term is decided on merit, not power. Quote the unsupported claim."},{"id":"ng-concessions","name":"Concession tracking","description":"Concessions and terms each side has offered or agreed to","prompt":"Track concessions and commitments on both sides: what each party has offered, conceded, or agreed to. Flag asymmetric exchanges where I ('me') gave more than I received. Summarize the current state of the deal."},{"id":"pushback","name":"When to push back","description":"One-sided terms, or vague over-promising / blurred focus you should pin down","prompt":"Identify moments where I ('me') should push back. Pushing back is NOT only arguing a term — it also means calling out vague over-promising or grand 'big-picture' pitches with no specifics, and pressing when the other party blurs focus or paints a rosy picture to dodge a hard point. Look for: one-sided terms, unreasonable demands, assumptions stated as facts, concessions extracted from me without reciprocity, or hand-wavy promises I should pin down. Flag it and suggest specifically what to push back on or what concrete commitment to ask for."},{"id":"leverage","name":"Options for mutual gain","description":"Trades on differently-valued issues that expand the pie","prompt":"Apply the principled-negotiation 'invent OPTIONS for mutual gain' principle: spot chances to EXPAND THE PIE rather than just split it — issues the two sides value DIFFERENTLY that can be traded, package deals, or contingent terms. Using the meeting context and MY stated target/direction, surface a concrete option ME can propose (what ME gives, what ME asks for in return) that moves toward MY goal while still being attractive to THEM — so ME negotiates on value, not just position."},{"id":"deception","name":"Deception","description":"Bad-faith manipulation, evasion, exaggeration, or pressure tactics from the other party","prompt":"You are monitoring the OTHER party ('them') for active DECEPTION or MANIPULATION (bad-faith tactics) — NOT mere inconsistency. Look for: evasive non-answers, bluffing, unverifiable grand claims, moving the goalposts, manufactured/false urgency, or pressure tactics meant to mislead or coerce. A legitimate constraint, an honest 'I don't know', or a stated change of position for a real reason is NOT deception. Flag only with concrete textual evidence; quote the suspicious lines."},{"id":"nextmove","name":"Next move","description":"Based on progress so far, what to say / ask / propose next","prompt":"Based on the conversation so far, recommend the single best next move for me ('me') to advance my goal — the specific question to ask, point to make, or term/number to propose right now. Make it concrete and say it in words I could use, plus one short line on why now. Only surface a new suggestion when the situation has meaningfully moved."}]},{"id":"tpl-rivalry","name":"Competitor talks","builtin":true,"evals":[{"id":"rv-leak","name":"What we gave away","description":"Information ME volunteered that a competitor can use, with nothing comparable back","prompt":"Watch what MY side gives away. Flag every moment ME volunteered information a competitor could use: roadmap, pricing structure, margins, customer names, headcount, timelines, weaknesses, or how badly ME needs this deal. Note whether THEM gave anything comparable in return — a one-sided disclosure is the finding, even when it felt like rapport."},{"id":"rv-probing","name":"They're fishing","description":"Questions about MY costs, customers, or capacity that go beyond this deal","prompt":"Detect THEM probing for intelligence rather than negotiating: questions about MY costs, customers, capacity, other deals, or internal plans that go beyond what this agreement needs. Flag each probe and what it is really after, so ME can decide what to answer."},{"id":"rv-commitment","name":"Lopsided commitments","description":"ME committing to something concrete against a deliberately vague answer","prompt":"Track the SYMMETRY of commitments. Flag when ME commits to something concrete (a date, a number, an exclusivity, a restriction) while THEM stays deliberately vague — 'we'd look at it', 'in principle', 'subject to internal approval'. Name the specific commitment ME made and the vague answer it bought."},{"id":"batna","name":"BATNA","description":"Each side's walk-away alternative — the real source of leverage","prompt":"Track BATNA (Best Alternative To a Negotiated Agreement) — each side's walk-away option, the true source of leverage. Using MY BATNA and bottom line from the setup, flag: signals about THEM's alternatives (strong or weak), moments THEM tests or probes MY alternative, and when the conversation pushes ME toward MY bottom line. Note who currently holds the stronger BATNA and what it means for MY leverage."},{"id":"deception","name":"Deception","description":"Bad-faith manipulation, evasion, exaggeration, or pressure tactics from the other party","prompt":"You are monitoring the OTHER party ('them') for active DECEPTION or MANIPULATION (bad-faith tactics) — NOT mere inconsistency. Look for: evasive non-answers, bluffing, unverifiable grand claims, moving the goalposts, manufactured/false urgency, or pressure tactics meant to mislead or coerce. A legitimate constraint, an honest 'I don't know', or a stated change of position for a real reason is NOT deception. Flag only with concrete textual evidence; quote the suspicious lines."},{"id":"inconsistency","name":"Inconsistency","description":"Genuine self-contradictions in what the other party said (not a stated change or a constraint)","prompt":"Track whether the OTHER party ('them') CONTRADICTS THEMSELVES: a later statement that genuinely conflicts with something they said earlier — a number, commitment, timeline, position, or fact that changed WITHOUT a stated reason. Flag only a real contradiction and cite BOTH conflicting quotes with their timestamps. A stated change of position for a legitimate reason, or a constraint/concern they raise (e.g. 'if I sign this as-is I'd breach a prior commitment'), is NOT an inconsistency — do not flag it."},{"id":"pushback","name":"When to push back","description":"One-sided terms, or vague over-promising / blurred focus you should pin down","prompt":"Identify moments where I ('me') should push back. Pushing back is NOT only arguing a term — it also means calling out vague over-promising or grand 'big-picture' pitches with no specifics, and pressing when the other party blurs focus or paints a rosy picture to dodge a hard point. Look for: one-sided terms, unreasonable demands, assumptions stated as facts, concessions extracted from me without reciprocity, or hand-wavy promises I should pin down. Flag it and suggest specifically what to push back on or what concrete commitment to ask for."},{"id":"topic-shift","name":"Topic drift","description":"Them changing the subject, answering a different question, or burying your point in irrelevant detail","prompt":"Watch for the other party ('them') steering away from the point: a sudden topic change, answering a different question than the one asked, retreating into vague generalities, or burying the issue under irrelevant detail — especially right after I ('me') raised something they'd rather avoid. When it happens, flag it, name the specific point they slid off, and suggest how I can steer back. This helps a less-experienced operator catch deflection in the moment."}]}],"todoTemplates":[{"id":"todo-interview","name":"Job interview","builtin":true,"items":["Introduce yourself and the role","Ask the candidate about their background and motivation","Dig into one representative project","Verify core technical skills / abilities","Ask about past conflicts and how they handled them","Leave time for the candidate's questions","Confirm salary expectations and start date","Explain next steps and timeline"]},{"id":"todo-salary","name":"Salary negotiation","builtin":true,"items":["Let them put out a number / range first","Cover the full package: base, bonus, equity, sign-on, benefits","State your value with market-rate evidence","Propose a justified target number (anchor)","Clarify equity terms (amount, valuation, vesting)","Confirm promotion / raise timeline and criteria","Handle pressure or artificial deadlines","Get a written offer and time to consider"]},{"id":"todo-sales-discovery","name":"Sales call","builtin":true,"items":["Confirm their role and decision authority","Understand the current situation and approach","Uncover the core pain and its impact","Quantify the cost / loss of the pain","Confirm the budget range","Clarify the decision process and key people","Understand timeline and urgency","Ask about existing solutions / competitors","Agree on a concrete next step"]},{"id":"todo-deal","name":"Deal-making","builtin":true,"items":["Confirm both sides' goals and walk-away (BATNA)","Clarify what they truly prioritize","Map out the variables: price, terms, timeline","Agree on the overall framework before details","Trade every concession for something of equal value","Record what's agreed and what's still open","Confirm the decision process and signing timeline","Summarize agreements and set the next step"]},{"id":"todo-diligence","name":"Diligence call","builtin":true,"items":["Confirm core financials and growth trends","Understand revenue mix and customer concentration","Check retention / churn and unit economics","Clarify competitive and market risks","Confirm the team, key people, and cap table","Review legal / compliance / IP status","Ask about tech debt and security posture","Request supporting documents and set a follow-up"]},{"id":"todo-coffee-chat","name":"Coffee chat (founder mentor)","builtin":true,"items":["Briefly introduce yourself and why you're here","Ask about their startup journey and key turning points","Ask about their biggest current challenge","Get their take on my current direction","Ask about common pitfalls and advice","Ask who's worth meeting / for intros","Ask for recommended resources or books","Agree on how to follow up next"]},{"id":"todo-fundraising","name":"Investor pitch","builtin":true,"items":["Explain what you do in one sentence","Lay out the problem and market size","Demo the product","Business model and key metrics (traction)","Introduce the team and why it's us","Competition and moat","Raise amount and use of funds","Confirm their investment range and decision process"]}],"delivery":{"pace":true,"pitch":false,"pauses":true,"tone":false},"syncEnabled":true,"defaultSaveLocation":{"scope":"personal","folderId":null},"gettingStarted":{"recorded":false,"filed":false,"replayed":false,"handedOff":false,"dismissedAt":1700000006000},"hintsSeen":["report.filing","replay.seek","copy.handoff","speakers.whoAmI","home.voiceTyping"],"provider":"openai"},"cloudAuth":{"token":"x","email":"y"},"drafts":[]},"version":4}"`;

exports[`store action trace > writes the persisted payload byte-identically for a fixed input 1`] = `"{"state":{"settings":{"language":"en","theme":"system","layout":"transcript","onboarded":false,"onboardingStep":0,"onboardingStepId":"","userName":"Fixed","userRole":"PM","userCompany":"","userBackground":"","aiMemoryNotes":"","aiMemoryUpdatedAt":0,"llmProviders":{"realtime":"groq","deep":"groq"},"anthropicApiKey":"","openaiApiKey":"","geminiApiKey":"","openrouterApiKey":"","groqApiKey":"","qwenApiKey":"","kimiApiKey":"","ollamaApiKey":"","parleyApiKey":"","customBaseUrl":"","customApiKey":"","reasoningEffort":{"realtime":"low","deep":"medium"},"models":{"anthropic":{"realtime":"claude-haiku-4-5","deep":"claude-opus-4-8"},"openai":{"realtime":"gpt-4.1-mini","deep":"gpt-5.5"},"gemini":{"realtime":"gemini-2.5-flash","deep":"gemini-2.5-pro"},"groq":{"realtime":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","deep":"openai/gpt-oss-120b"},"qwen":{"realtime":"qwen-plus","deep":"qwen-max"},"kimi":{"realtime":"kimi-k2-turbo-preview","deep":"kimi-k2-thinking"},"ollama":{"realtime":"llama3.2","deep":"qwen3"},"openrouter":{"realtime":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","deep":"openai/gpt-5.5"},"parley":{"realtime":"parley-fast","deep":"parley-smart"},"custom":{"realtime":"","deep":""}},"transcriptionProvider":"soniox","sonioxApiKey":"","deepgramApiKey":"","assemblyaiApiKey":"","localSttModel":"whisper-large-v3-turbo-q5_0","localSttModelChosen":false,"inputDevice":"","autoStudyAnalysis":true,"voiceTypingEnabled":true,"voiceTypingShortcut":"combo:control+alt+Space","voiceTypingMode":"hold","voiceTypingPolishStyle":"tidy","voiceTypingRestoreClipboard":false,"evaluations":[{"id":"in-undecided","name":"False consensus","description":"Things the room treated as settled without actually settling them","prompt":"Watch for topics the room TREATED as settled without actually settling them: a proposal met with 'sure' or silence and never confirmed, two people agreeing to different things in the same breath, or a decision announced while an unanswered objection was still on the table. Flag each one and name the specific thing that still needs an explicit decision. A genuine, explicit agreement is NOT a finding."},{"id":"in-unowned","name":"Unowned work","description":"Follow-ups the meeting created with no named owner or deadline","prompt":"Track work the meeting created and whether anyone actually took it. Flag every task, follow-up, or investigation that was agreed but left with NO named owner, no deadline, or an owner who never acknowledged it ('someone should…', 'we need to…'). Quote the line where the work appeared."}],"evalTemplates":[{"id":"tpl-internal","name":"Internal meeting","builtin":true,"evals":[{"id":"in-undecided","name":"False consensus","description":"Things the room treated as settled without actually settling them","prompt":"Watch for topics the room TREATED as settled without actually settling them: a proposal met with 'sure' or silence and never confirmed, two people agreeing to different things in the same breath, or a decision announced while an unanswered objection was still on the table. Flag each one and name the specific thing that still needs an explicit decision. A genuine, explicit agreement is NOT a finding."},{"id":"in-unowned","name":"Unowned work","description":"Follow-ups the meeting created with no named owner or deadline","prompt":"Track work the meeting created and whether anyone actually took it. Flag every task, follow-up, or investigation that was agreed but left with NO named owner, no deadline, or an owner who never acknowledged it ('someone should…', 'we need to…'). Quote the line where the work appeared."},{"id":"in-scope","name":"Scope creep","description":"Additions folded into existing work with no cost weighed and no date moved","prompt":"Watch for scope quietly growing: new requirements, extra cases, or 'while we're in there' additions folded into existing work without anyone weighing the cost or moving a date. Flag what was added and what it was added onto, so the trade-off gets made deliberately instead of by accident."},{"id":"in-blocked","name":"Dependencies and blockers","description":"Work waiting on someone else, and blockers nobody was assigned to clear","prompt":"Surface dependencies and blockers named in the meeting: work waiting on another person, team, decision, or external party. Flag each with what is blocked and what it is waiting on. Also flag a blocker that was mentioned in passing and never assigned to anyone to unblock."},{"id":"unanswered","name":"Unanswered questions","description":"Questions I asked that they dodged or never answered directly","prompt":"Track questions I ('me') asked that the other party did NOT clearly answer — they deflected, gave a vague response, or changed the subject. Flag each open question so I can re-ask it. Quote my original question and their evasive reply."},{"id":"checklist","name":"Process gaps","description":"Standard topics for this meeting type that haven't been covered yet","prompt":"Given the meeting context provided, identify important topics or questions that are standard for this kind of meeting but have NOT yet been covered. Flag what's missing so I can raise it before the meeting ends."}]},{"id":"tpl-sales","name":"Sales call","builtin":true,"evals":[{"id":"sl-qualification","name":"Qualification gaps (MEDDICC)","description":"MEDDICC dimensions still unclear: Metrics, economic buyer, decision criteria, pain, process, Champion","prompt":"You are helping qualify a sales opportunity. Track the MEDDICC-style dimensions: quantified Metrics, Economic buyer, Decision criteria, Decision process, identified Pain, and a Champion. Flag which dimensions are still unknown or weak so I ('me') can ask about them before the call ends."},{"id":"sl-pain","name":"Pain depth & urgency","description":"Whether their pain is specific, quantified, and urgent","prompt":"Assess the prospect's pain. Flag when their problem is stated vaguely, is not quantified (cost, time, risk), or lacks urgency / a compelling event. Suggest the specific question that would deepen or quantify the pain."},{"id":"sl-objections","name":"Objections","description":"Objections or concerns they raise, flagging any not yet addressed","prompt":"Detect objections or concerns the prospect ('them') raises — price, timing, fit, competitor, risk, authority. Flag each one, and especially any that I ('me') have NOT yet addressed. Quote the objection."},{"id":"claims","name":"Claims to verify","description":"Verifiable factual claims by the other party, flagged to check later","prompt":"Extract concrete, verifiable factual claims made by the other party ('them') — numbers, dates, credentials, references, commitments. These are things worth fact-checking later. List each claim. Severity is informational unless a claim is central to the deal/decision."},{"id":"unanswered","name":"Unanswered questions","description":"Questions I asked that they dodged or never answered directly","prompt":"Track questions I ('me') asked that the other party did NOT clearly answer — they deflected, gave a vague response, or changed the subject. Flag each open question so I can re-ask it. Quote my original question and their evasive reply."},{"id":"nextmove","name":"Next move","description":"Based on progress so far, what to say / ask / propose next","prompt":"Based on the conversation so far, recommend the single best next move for me ('me') to advance my goal — the specific question to ask, point to make, or term/number to propose right now. Make it concrete and say it in words I could use, plus one short line on why now. Only surface a new suggestion when the situation has meaningfully moved."}]},{"id":"tpl-pricing","name":"Price negotiation","builtin":true,"evals":[{"id":"zopa","name":"Zone of agreement","description":"The overlap of acceptable ranges — is an offer inside the zone","prompt":"Map the ZOPA (Zone Of Possible Agreement) on the key terms (price, scope, timing, equity, …): track what each side reveals about their acceptable range versus MY target and bottom line from the setup. Flag when an offer falls OUTSIDE the likely ZOPA, when the revealed ranges OVERLAP (a deal is reachable), or when a number is still missing to locate the zone. Be concrete about which term and the implied range."},{"id":"batna","name":"BATNA","description":"Each side's walk-away alternative — the real source of leverage","prompt":"Track BATNA (Best Alternative To a Negotiated Agreement) — each side's walk-away option, the true source of leverage. Using MY BATNA and bottom line from the setup, flag: signals about THEM's alternatives (strong or weak), moments THEM tests or probes MY alternative, and when the conversation pushes ME toward MY bottom line. Note who currently holds the stronger BATNA and what it means for MY leverage."},{"id":"criteria","name":"Objective criteria","description":"Decide terms by objective standards, not will or pressure","prompt":"Apply 'insist on OBJECTIVE CRITERIA'. Flag when a number or term is justified by will, pressure, or 'that's just our policy' rather than an objective standard (market rate, precedent, independent benchmark, a formula). Name the objective criterion ME could anchor to so the term is decided on merit, not power. Quote the unsupported claim."},{"id":"ng-concessions","name":"Concession tracking","description":"Concessions and terms each side has offered or agreed to","prompt":"Track concessions and commitments on both sides: what each party has offered, conceded, or agreed to. Flag asymmetric exchanges where I ('me') gave more than I received. Summarize the current state of the deal."},{"id":"pushback","name":"When to push back","description":"One-sided terms, or vague over-promising / blurred focus you should pin down","prompt":"Identify moments where I ('me') should push back. Pushing back is NOT only arguing a term — it also means calling out vague over-promising or grand 'big-picture' pitches with no specifics, and pressing when the other party blurs focus or paints a rosy picture to dodge a hard point. Look for: one-sided terms, unreasonable demands, assumptions stated as facts, concessions extracted from me without reciprocity, or hand-wavy promises I should pin down. Flag it and suggest specifically what to push back on or what concrete commitment to ask for."},{"id":"leverage","name":"Options for mutual gain","description":"Trades on differently-valued issues that expand the pie","prompt":"Apply the principled-negotiation 'invent OPTIONS for mutual gain' principle: spot chances to EXPAND THE PIE rather than just split it — issues the two sides value DIFFERENTLY that can be traded, package deals, or contingent terms. Using the meeting context and MY stated target/direction, surface a concrete option ME can propose (what ME gives, what ME asks for in return) that moves toward MY goal while still being attractive to THEM — so ME negotiates on value, not just position."},{"id":"deception","name":"Deception","description":"Bad-faith manipulation, evasion, exaggeration, or pressure tactics from the other party","prompt":"You are monitoring the OTHER party ('them') for active DECEPTION or MANIPULATION (bad-faith tactics) — NOT mere inconsistency. Look for: evasive non-answers, bluffing, unverifiable grand claims, moving the goalposts, manufactured/false urgency, or pressure tactics meant to mislead or coerce. A legitimate constraint, an honest 'I don't know', or a stated change of position for a real reason is NOT deception. Flag only with concrete textual evidence; quote the suspicious lines."},{"id":"nextmove","name":"Next move","description":"Based on progress so far, what to say / ask / propose next","prompt":"Based on the conversation so far, recommend the single best next move for me ('me') to advance my goal — the specific question to ask, point to make, or term/number to propose right now. Make it concrete and say it in words I could use, plus one s