the stronger BATNA and what it means for MY leverage."},{"id":"deception","name":"Deception","description":"Bad-faith manipulation, evasion, exaggeration, or pressure tactics from the other party","prompt":"You are monitoring the OTHER party ('them') for active DECEPTION or MANIPULATION (bad-faith tactics) — NOT mere inconsistency. Look for: evasive non-answers, bluffing, unverifiable grand claims, moving the goalposts, manufactured/false urgency, or pressure tactics meant to mislead or coerce. A legitimate constraint, an honest 'I don't know', or a stated change of position for a real reason is NOT deception. Flag only with concrete textual evidence; quote the suspicious lines."},{"id":"inconsistency","name":"Inconsistency","description":"Genuine self-contradictions in what the other party said (not a stated change or a constraint)","prompt":"Track whether the OTHER party ('them') CONTRADICTS THEMSELVES: a later statement that genuinely conflicts with something they said earlier — a number, commitment, timeline, position, or fact that changed WITHOUT a stated reason. Flag only a real contradiction and cite BOTH conflicting quotes with their timestamps. A stated change of position for a legitimate reason, or a constraint/concern they raise (e.g. 'if I sign this as-is I'd breach a prior commitment'), is NOT an inconsistency — do not flag it."},{"id":"pushback","name":"When to push back","description":"One-sided terms, or vague over-promising / blurred focus you should pin down","prompt":"Identify moments where I ('me') should push back. Pushing back is NOT only arguing a term — it also means calling out vague over-promising or grand 'big-picture' pitches with no specifics, and pressing when the other party blurs focus or paints a rosy picture to dodge a hard point. Look for: one-sided terms, unreasonable demands, assumptions stated as facts, concessions extracted from me without reciprocity, or hand-wavy promises I should pin down. Flag it and suggest specifically what to push back on or what concrete commitment to ask for."},{"id":"topic-shift","name":"Topic drift","description":"Them changing the subject, answering a different question, or burying your point in irrelevant detail","prompt":"Watch for the other party ('them') steering away from the point: a sudden topic change, answering a different question than the one asked, retreating into vague generalities, or burying the issue under irrelevant detail — especially right after I ('me') raised something they'd rather avoid. When it happens, flag it, name the specific point they slid off, and suggest how I can steer back. This helps a less-experienced operator catch deflection in the moment."}]}],"todoTemplates":[{"id":"todo-interview","name":"Job interview","builtin":true,"items":["Introduce yourself and the role","Ask the candidate about their background and motivation","Dig into one representative project","Verify core technical skills / abilities","Ask about past conflicts and how they handled them","Leave time for the candidate's questions","Confirm salary expectations and start date","Explain next steps and timeline"]},{"id":"todo-salary","name":"Salary negotiation","builtin":true,"items":["Let them put out a number / range first","Cover the full package: base, bonus, equity, sign-on, benefits","State your value with market-rate evidence","Propose a justified target number (anchor)","Clarify equity terms (amount, valuation, vesting)","Confirm promotion / raise timeline and criteria","Handle pressure or artificial deadlines","Get a written offer and time to consider"]},{"id":"todo-sales-discovery","name":"Sales call","builtin":true,"items":["Confirm their role and decision authority","Understand the current situation and approach","Uncover the core pain and its impact","Quantify the cost / loss of the pain","Confirm the budget range","Clarify the decision process and key people","Understand timeline and urgency","Ask about existing solutions / competitors","Agree on a concrete next step"]},{"id":"todo-deal","name":"Deal-making","builtin":true,"items":["Confirm both sides' goals and walk-away (BATNA)","Clarify what they truly prioritize","Map out the variables: price, terms, timeline","Agree on the overall framework before details","Trade every concession for something of equal value","Record what's agreed and what's still open","Confirm the decision process and signing timeline","Summarize agreements and set the next step"]},{"id":"todo-diligence","name":"Diligence call","builtin":true,"items":["Confirm core financials and growth trends","Understand revenue mix and customer concentration","Check retention / churn and unit economics","Clarify competitive and market risks","Confirm the team, key people, and cap table","Review legal / compliance / IP status","Ask about tech debt and security posture","Request supporting documents and set a follow-up"]},{"id":"todo-coffee-chat","name":"Coffee chat (founder mentor)","builtin":true,"items":["Briefly introduce yourself and why you're here","Ask about their startup journey and key turning points","Ask about their biggest current challenge","Get their take on my current direction","Ask about common pitfalls and advice","Ask who's worth meeting / for intros","Ask for recommended resources or books","Agree on how to follow up next"]},{"id":"todo-fundraising","name":"Investor pitch","builtin":true,"items":["Explain what you do in one sentence","Lay out the problem and market size","Demo the product","Business model and key metrics (traction)","Introduce the team and why it's us","Competition and moat","Raise amount and use of funds","Confirm their investment range and decision process"]}],"delivery":{"pace":true,"pitch":false,"pauses":true,"tone":false},"syncEnabled":true,"defaultSaveLocation":{"scope":"personal","folderId":null},"gettingStarted":{"recorded":false,"filed":false,"replayed":false,"handedOff":false,"dismissedAt":null},"hintsSeen":[]},"cloudAuth":{"token":"tok","email":"a@b"},"dr